335
00:40:09,195 --> 00:40:14,215
And now you start feeling something called FOMO, or Fear of Missing Out.

336
00:40:15,215 --> 00:40:21,576
FOMO is the anxiety we experience when we feel there's something exciting happening elsewhere, and we're not a part of it.

337
00:40:21,576 --> 00:40:27,815
It's been around for a long time, but these days it's triggered mostly by posts on social media.

338
00:40:29,375 --> 00:40:32,895
Social media gives us instant access to the activity of our friends.

339
00:40:32,895 --> 00:40:34,496
That's what it's there for.

340
00:40:35,155 --> 00:40:41,255
And this can be a good thing, but it also makes it all too easy for us to compare our lives to theirs.

341
00:40:42,295 --> 00:40:46,295
This can lead us to second-guessing our decisions and feeling insecure in general.

342
00:40:46,295 --> 00:40:51,775
It can even get to the point when there's a looming sense of FOMO even when we're not online.

343
00:40:52,735 --> 00:40:54,295
So how do we kick this FOMO?

344
00:40:55,175 --> 00:40:59,375
An answer that might quickly spring to mind is to simply quit social media.

345
00:41:00,076 --> 00:41:02,476
But that's not practical for a lot of people.

346
00:41:03,416 --> 00:41:08,255
Instead of quitting, you can try limiting your time on it, or even just taking a few days off.

347
00:41:08,916 --> 00:41:11,815
This can give you a chance to focus on what's important in your life,

348
00:41:11,815 --> 00:41:15,155
and enjoy the things that you are doing without comparing them to others.

349
00:41:16,596 --> 00:41:20,056
The lives of our friends do sometimes look pretty exciting online.

350
00:41:20,615 --> 00:41:23,655
But let's put some quotation marks around the word lives.

351
00:41:24,456 --> 00:41:27,655
Their social media activity isn't their actual life, per se.

352
00:41:28,295 --> 00:41:32,996
It's more of a highlight reel of exciting things they've posted to contribute to their online identity.

353
00:41:33,735 --> 00:41:35,795
